  "articleBody": "Sometimes, a kitchen refresh in a foreclosed property goes beyond a simple DIY paint job, and that's when a professional really becomes essential. If you notice any active leaks, even small ones, that's a clear sign. Water damage can lead to mold and structural problems quickly, so it needs to be addressed correctly by an expert. Suspected mold is another big one; proper remediation is crucial for health and safety. Damaged or faulty wiring is a huge safety hazard and definitely calls for a licensed electrician, which a good general contractor can coordinate. If the floors feel soft or spongy, or you see warped framing around cabinets or windows, these are signs of potential structural issues that need professional assessment and repair. Essentially, any indication that your kitchen refresh might involve more than just surface updates – meaning it requires plumbing, electrical, or structural work – means it's time to bring in the pros. They have the experience to diagnose complex problems, ensure everything is up to code, and prevent costly mistakes down the road. HH Remodeling LLC has the expertise to handle these deeper issues, making sure your kitchen is not just pretty, but safe and sound.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}